   Interesting...
...is the message you get when trying to #dip corrodeable stuff in acid,
at the moment. Why is that? Shouldn't potions of acid corrode things just
as much as acid traps or acidic monster attacks? This looks like a 
deliberate decision by the DevTeam, though, so I'm confused.


> What other potions ought to have effects on the stuff under them? Polymorph, 
> I guess, and oil, and !Invis and !SeeInvis if the "invisible
> objects" patch is applied... any more?

   I decided against making !Poly do anything other than a YAUM (Yet 
Another Useful Message), because I realized that accidentally polying
a shopkeeper's inventory would be an instadeath for the player, and
that would be mean. So instead of polymorphing, objects splashed by !Poly
just "shimmer for a moment," with no effect on gameplay except that a
spoiled player will now be able to identify !Poly that way.

   Why doesn't hitting an invisible monster with a !SeeInvisible make
the monster visible?  Sure, it's not realistic; but given the amount of
wordplay around wands of undead turning, it's not particularly 
far-fetched. Anyway, the "invisible objects" patch gives !SeeInvisible
that kind of behavior for objects, so I've preserved it in my "splashing"
patch.

